Cross-module reference nested inside a `:not(...)` pseudo-class payload.
The recursion through `transform_pseudoclass_kind` carries the sentinel
into the nested selector position, and the aggregator's substitution
pass operates on rendered strings so it doesn't care about CSS structure.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml m.re > m.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl m.ml -o m.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml n.re > n.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl n.ml -o n.ml

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml n.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_392d75,._t1_392d75:not(x-),._t2_392d75:not(x-):not(x-){background:blue;}
  ._a_656tv39kode:disabled:not(._a_656tv39kode._id_144nxwi),._t1_656tv39kode:not(x-):disabled:not(._t1_656tv39kode._id_144nxwi),._t2_656tv39kode:not(x-):not(x-):disabled:not(._t2_656tv39kode._id_144nxwi){background:gray;}
